Open compliance question
------------------------

Apache-2.0 section 4(b) asks for prominent notices on files that have been
modified. This fork currently satisfies attribution through this NOTICE, the git
history of the fork, and the retained LICENSE.txt, rather than through a per-file
header. Min itself ships no per-file copyright headers, so adding them would mean
introducing a new convention across the tree.

The strict reading of 4(b) - that every modified file carries a notice - has not
been adopted. It is recorded here as unresolved rather than as settled, so it can
be decided deliberately before anything is published widely.
